# Philont example environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
# Only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is strictly required; everything else has sane defaults.

# ── Main model (Anthropic-compatible) ───────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Custom / proxy endpoint (defaults to https://api.anthropic.com)
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# Model id (defaults to a current Claude model)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
#
# Provider switch. Default 'anthropic' uses the ANTHROPIC_* config above
# (Anthropic Messages protocol — Claude, or DeepSeek's /anthropic endpoint).
# Set to an OpenAI-compatible provider to use those instead:
#   LLM_PROVIDER=openai     # generic; OPENAI_BASE_URL reaches ANY compatible endpoint
#     OPENAI_API_KEY=...  OPENAI_MODEL=...  OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
#   LLM_PROVIDER=glm        # 智谱; GLM_API_KEY / GLM_MODEL (base url built in)
#   LLM_PROVIDER=kimi       # Moonshot; KIMI_API_KEY / KIMI_MODEL
#   LLM_PROVIDER=minimax    # MINIMAX_API_KEY / MINIMAX_MODEL
#   LLM_PROVIDER=gemini     # GEMINI_API_KEY / GEMINI_MODEL (Google OpenAI-compat)
# Internally philont always uses Anthropic message structure; OpenAI-compatible
# providers are translated both ways automatically.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# ── Auxiliary small model — the SECOND OPINION (recommended) ────────────────
# Used for cheap distillation (web-fetch summarization, reflection) AND as the
# independent second model: it reviews a guide-driven plan against the guide, it
# classifies intent and authorization replies, and it scores the learning judge.
# Falls back to the main model when unset — but with no aux configured the plan
# REVIEWER does not exist at all, and plan verification degrades to its
# deterministic coverage check alone. A small/cheap model is fine here; being a
# DIFFERENT model matters more than being a bigger one.
# Protocol: openai | anthropic.
# BASE_URL accepts the same address as the main model: a bare host
# (https://api.deepseek.com), a versioned base (…/v1), or the full endpoint.
# AUX_LLM_BASE_URL=
# AUX_LLM_API_KEY=
# AUX_LLM_MODEL=
# AUX_LLM_PROTOCOL=openai

# ── Vision (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The `vision` tool needs a MULTIMODAL model. If your main model isn't multimodal
# (e.g. DeepSeek), point vision at a dedicated multimodal model here — independent
# of the main model. Supports both OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic protocols.
# VISION_LLM_BASE_URL=
# VISION_LLM_API_KEY=
# VISION_LLM_MODEL=
# Protocol: openai (default) | anthropic. Auto-detected from the base URL if unset
# (URLs containing "anthropic" -> anthropic). Most domestic multimodal models
# (Qwen-VL, GLM-4V, Step, MiniMax) are OpenAI-compatible -> leave as openai.
# VISION_LLM_PROTOCOL=openai
#
# Examples:
#   Qwen-VL (DashScope, OpenAI-compatible):
#     VISION_LLM_BASE_URL=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#     VISION_LLM_MODEL=qwen-vl-max
#   GLM-4V (Zhipu, OpenAI-compatible):
#     VISION_LLM_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
#     VISION_LLM_MODEL=glm-4v
#   Claude (Anthropic protocol):
#     VISION_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
#     VISION_LLM_PROTOCOL=anthropic
#     VISION_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# ── Tools / capabilities (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Enable browser automation via Playwright MCP (local stdio, no extra account).
# PHILONT_MCP_BROWSER=1
# Path to an MCP server config file (default: ~/.philont/mcp.json)
# PHILONT_MCP_CONFIG=
# Web search backend key (if your webSearch tool uses Brave).
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# ── Deep reasoning (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deep_explore tool (multi-step conjecture attack via an internal mini-loop
# with reason_decompose/reason_record + local retrieval) is ON by default.
# Set to 0 to disable it.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE=0
# Per-round LLM<->tool turn cap inside one deep_explore round (default 40, 5-100).
# Raise it when hard problems get cut off before they unfold.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_MAX_ITERS=40
# Cross-turn token budget for one reasoning session (default 300000, min 50000).
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_TOKEN_BUDGET=300000
# Wall-clock budget per reasoning round (default 720000 = 12min, min 30000). Kept
# safely under the 20min turn hard deadline so a long round stops gracefully (tree
# saved, resumable via "continue") instead of hitting TurnDeadlineError.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_ROUND_DEADLINE_MS=720000
# Checkable-object tooth (ON by default; =0 disables). A settle whose claim contains something a machine
# can DECIDE — a determinant value, a symbolic identity, an explicit point and its claimed image, a
# primality claim — is refused ONCE, naming the tool that decides it, if nothing has been computed in the
# session yet. Checkability is a property of the CLAIM, not of the session mode, so this applies to an
# evidence-based (deliberate) session too: that is where an explicit polynomial map was once settled on
# citations while pariGp sat unused. The second attempt on the same node goes through with a caveat, so a
# false positive costs one iteration and can never wedge a session.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_VERIFY_OBJECTS=1
# Refutation pairing (ON by default; =0 disables). A universally quantified or conjecture-shaped goal is
# seeded, before the first round, with one extra node: "no counterexample exists inside an explicitly
# stated bounded region". Proving a for-all statement needs an ARGUMENT (no finite check settles it);
# disproving it needs ONE WITNESS, which a machine can decide — so this side is always checkable, and a
# session can no longer spend its whole life on a tree where nothing produces a signal (the observed
# 14-round no-progress shape). It is an ordinary open node: the model may work it, defer it, or close it
# as a dead end. Decision/preference goals are never paired — nothing there could be refuted by a witness.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_REFUTATION_NODE=1

# ── Channels (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Telegram bot channel. Create a bot with @BotFather to get the token.
# TELEGRAM_ENABLED=1
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-DEF...
# DM access: open (default) | allowlist | disabled. With allowlist, set the
# numeric Telegram user id(s) allowed to talk to the bot.
# TELEGRAM_DM_POLICY=open
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=11111111,22222222
# Group access: open (default) | allowlist | disabled.
# TELEGRAM_GROUP_POLICY=open
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_GROUPS=-1001234567890
# Proxy for api.telegram.org (Telegram is blocked in some regions). Applies ONLY
# to the Telegram channel — domestic services keep direct connections. Falls back
# to HTTPS_PROXY / ALL_PROXY if unset. e.g. a local Clash HTTP proxy:
# TELEGRAM_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
#
# WeChat channel. First scan-login via `npm run wechat:login`.
# WECHAT_ENABLED=1
# DM access: open (default) | allowlist | disabled. NOTE: with allowlist and
# WECHAT_DM_POLICY=open
# WECHAT_ALLOWED_USERS=o9cq8xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx@im.wechat
# Group access: open (default) | allowlist | disabled.
# WECHAT_GROUP_POLICY=open
# WECHAT_ALLOWED_GROUPS=

# ── Memory / runtime (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite memory database path (default: ~/.philont/memory/memory.sqlite)
# MEMORY_DB_PATH=
# Kill switch for the idle-time autonomous loop (1 = on, 0 = off; default on).
# PHILONT_AUTONOMOUS=1
# Per-day LLM token ceiling for the autonomous loop; once hit it skips the rest of
# the day's ticks ("daily token cap reached" in the logs). Set a number to cap idle
# spend; 0 = unlimited (default).
# PHILONT_AUTONOMOUS_DAILY_TOKENS=0
# First-contact push auto-subscribe (default on): the first DM from a peer on WeChat/Telegram
# creates a push subscription (with an opt-out notice in the same turn), so proactive digests
# and urgent findings can actually reach you. A previous unsubscribe is always respected.
# PHILONT_PUSH_AUTOSUBSCRIBE=1
# ── Selfhood closure (docs/design/selfhood_closure.md) — all default on, =0 disables ────────
# Live personality: traits derived from the agent's own history (drive effectiveness, curiosity
# payoff) tune goal-loop promotion and stuck thresholds. Off = frozen neutral defaults.
# PHILONT_TRAITS_LIVE=1
# Self-observations: behavioral tendencies aggregated from the action/drive ledger into self
# facts (obs.*, evidence refs mandatory), injected as "What I know about my own tendencies".
# PHILONT_SELF_OBSERVATIONS=1
# Recipe reuse verification: a callable recipe that fails within its own tool-policy scope on
# reuse is demoted to an advisory lesson (and recorded as a self-observation).
# PHILONT_RECIPE_REUSE_VERIFY=1
# Skill self-repair (ON by default — docs/design/skill_self_repair.md; set to 0 to disable). The idle
# loop picks up a recipe that RECIPE_REUSE_VERIFY demoted, diagnoses it from its real failed runs in the
# execution ledger (one single-turn LLM call, no tools), and rewrites its steps — the old version is kept
# in revision_history and the recipe re-enters at 'draft' to re-earn trust through real reuse. A recipe
# that resists 3 repairs stops being proposed. It is the only autonomous driver that rewrites a reusable
# artifact, so it keeps its own switch and hard rails: the diagnosis prompt forbids OS-assuming /
# privileged / system-mutating fixes, and an inconclusive diagnosis rewrites nothing (recipe stays advisory).
# PHILONT_SKILL_REPAIR=1
# Constitution proposals: the agent may PROPOSE identity amendments with evidence; only the
# owner's explicit approval applies them (append-only, red lines never amendable).
# PHILONT_CONSTITUTION_PROPOSALS=1
# Capability manifest (ON by default; set to 0 to stop the per-turn injection — the self_capabilities
# tool stays available either way). Each turn a compact block of "what you can do right now" is injected,
# GENERATED from live runtime state (feature flags + registered autonomous drivers + tool count), never
# hand-written — so the agent self-assesses against the current build instead of a stale memory of itself.
# PHILONT_CAPABILITY_MANIFEST=1
# Conscience gate (off by default): when on, every outbound message to a human (WeChat/Telegram)
# is first judged by one LLM call against a short safety constitution (no harm to people:
# defamation/doxxing/disinformation/harm-enabling instructions). Fail-open — if the judge errors
# or times out, the message is sent. Adds one LLM call of latency/cost per reply when enabled.
# PHILONT_CONSCIENCE_GATE=off
# Three-tier deep_explore routing by intent-router confidence (2026-07-09):
#   conf >= FORCE_CONF -> the harness guarantees deep_explore(start) even if the model answers flat;
#   ASK_CONF <= conf < FORCE_CONF -> one question first ("进"/"直接"), the reply decides;
#   conf < ASK_CONF -> direct flat execution (no nudge).
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_FORCE_CONF=0.9
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_ASK_CONF=0.7
# Background auto-advance for deep_explore. The global flag is ON by default, but nothing runs
# until a session is explicitly committed (deep_explore auto_on) — the per-session opt-in is the
# real gate. When armed, the session advances round-by-round in the background — no need to keep
# typing "continue" — and progress is pushed proactively; it stops on solved or after a few stuck rounds.
# PHILONT_DEEP_EXPLORE_AUTO_ADVANCE=1
# IANA timezone for scheduling / time display (default: system).
# AGENT_TIMEZONE=Asia/Singapore
# Agent server HTTP + WebSocket port (default: 20266). The launcher injects this.
# PHILONT_PORT=20266

# ── Compass — where your second mind points (optional) ──────────────────────
# compass.md is the owner-authored source for the intrinsic drives and focus.
# It lives next to compass.example.md in philont's own directory and is CREATED
# FOR YOU from that template on first start; it is git-ignored, so `git pull`
# never clobbers your edits. Restart after editing (no hot reload yet).
# Drive lines set a baseline AND a leash — live trait tuning can move inside
# [min,max] but never past it. Focus lines are seeded as pursuits, which is what
# the background self-drive actually selects from. No compass = neutral defaults
# (unbounded auto-tuning, no declared focus). Override the location here:
# PHILONT_COMPASS_PATH=

# ── Language (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The owner's declared language: zh | en | auto (default auto; normally set from
# the web-ui). Resolution is: AGENT_LANGUAGE > the observed user.locale fact >
# channel > mirror the user's own message. A declaration outranks an inference —
# and it is the ONLY source on a turn with no user message, i.e. a proactive push
# where the agent speaks first with nothing to mirror.
# AGENT_LANGUAGE=auto

# ── Plan loop / service guards (optional) ───────────────────────────────────
# The deterministic plan state machine for a task that ships with a written guide
# (DRAFT -> VERIFY -> REVISE -> EXECUTE -> computed CLOSE). ON by default; =0
# falls back to the legacy placeholder + gate path.
# PHILONT_PLAN_LOOP=1
# Compile a service's prose guide into an authoritative contract via the aux LLM.
# OFF by default (=1 to enable). Rationale: a wrong CALL is corrected by the
# service (404/401/400 are free and exact), but a wrong CONTRACT has nothing to
# correct it, because the contract IS the corrector. What is kept without it: the
# deterministic regex anchor + host allowlist (a wrong host is the one error the
# service cannot report), guide coverage via the two-model review loop, and the
# replayable service skill emitted from the run's VERIFIED calls.
# PHILONT_SPEC_COMPILE=0
# Id-provenance guard: refuse a write whose identifier appears in nothing the
# agent actually read this turn (task text + every successful tool result). ON by
# default, scoped to the plan loop's own tool runner; =0 disables it.
# PHILONT_ID_PROVENANCE=1
# Shell/process command gate: full | publish | off (default full).
#   full    = hard-deny catastrophic shapes and require a narrow approval for
#             destructive local commands plus publishing/remote/credential changes.
#   publish = keep hard denies and approval gates whose effects leave the machine
#             (git push, remote/credential changes, curl|sh); allow the local
#             destructive require-grant tail without a card.
#   off     = keep hard denies only; disable every require-grant command pattern.
# This does NOT disable the sensitive-path validator or the validator-only floor.
# Lowering this setting materially weakens application-level protection.
# PHILONT_COMMAND_GATE=full

# ── Self-learning (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The learning judge scores each turn as success / failure / could_not_verify so
# skills can later be crystallized from VERIFIED successes instead of online
# attribution proxies. ON by default but SHADOW ONLY today: it logs
# ([learning-judge] shadow verdict=…) and drives nothing. `success` requires a
# successful GROUNDING tool (shell/http/prover) — never a bystander readFile —
# and it fails safe to could_not_verify whenever the aux model is unavailable.
# PHILONT_LEARNING_JUDGE=1
# Replay a learned repair against the past failure it came from, on idle, so a rule that was learned
# once and never applied stops being indistinguishable from one that does not work (default OFF).
# PHILONT_REPAIR_REPLAY=1
# Which tools may be replayed unattended. Only tools whose effect is confined to producing an answer.
# PHILONT_REPAIR_REPLAY_TOOLS=pariGp,z3Verify,leanCheck
# Apply a learned mechanical-failure rule and retry the same tool once (default on).
# Set to 0/off to disable retries while keeping recurrence measurement active.
# PHILONT_MECHANICAL_REPAIR=1
# Session-claim adjudicator (ON by default; =0 leaves the pattern floor). When the runtime knows there is
# NO reasoning session and no deep_explore call succeeded, but the reply is long enough to have narrated
# one, the aux model is asked a plain reading-comprehension question: does this text state that a session
# exists? A word list cannot answer that — the one written for it immediately mis-read "No deep_explore
# session is running" as a claim that one WAS. The patterns stay as an always-on floor; this is the
# ceiling, and it returns "unknown" on every failure path, so an absent aux costs nothing.
# PHILONT_HONESTY_SESSION_ADJUDICATOR=1

# ── Network proxy (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Global outbound proxy. When set, ALL fetch-based traffic (Claude API, aux model,
# webFetch/webSearch/downloadFile, WeChat, Telegram) is routed through it via
# undici's global dispatcher. Telegram can still override with TELEGRAM_PROXY.
# Standard HTTPS_PROXY / ALL_PROXY are also honored. Note: no NO_PROXY allowlist
# yet — a global proxy also routes domestic LLM gateways through it.
# PHILONT_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
